{"id": "EUVD-2026-103735", "enisaUuid": "811d7df3-f5d5-3c8e-b771-4386ad08605b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: arp: terminate device name before lookup\n\nThe ARP ioctl copies a user-provided struct arpreq into a stack object. Its\narp_dev field may contain IFNAMSIZ bytes without a NUL terminator.\n\nSuch input is passed to dev_get_by_name_rcu() or __dev_get_by_name(), where\nstrcmp() can read past the end of the stack object when a matching\nalternative interface name exists.\n\nTerminate the field before the lookup to prevent the out-of-bounds read.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:16:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:20:32", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ae6d704dbf9542b0a0830ec91a2db4f30307e7d8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/47107491b48ceef0a2faa7a010cfa961f211ef9f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7389757d88f54237951d7497d9c4dae7cc6d64be", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1b08c5c3ac27c9ff91c5309f4a32b4e91ce2263b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/414bbad9928598904313299ac9e037a73f520be1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ba664d83638640cf454b65167339cbf20dfd6f10", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/35e716a70733472ede300540082d64c33bf3b4c9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d8b6529e80bcb4fb8177121404cbb3377acaebd2"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98495", "GHSA-qjmq-cw92-j553"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c1a71c9-809a-3638-aca0-c11ac7b835d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "36fbf1e52bd3ff8a5cb604955eedfc9350c2e6cc <1b08c5c3ac27c9ff91c5309f4a32b4e91ce2263b"}, {"id": "0ed54d7b-e239-3c14-b4a2-6725c2f23174", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "182fe773-dde8-3487-bcd9-b93bbd8e083f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "36fbf1e52bd3ff8a5cb604955eedfc9350c2e6cc <ae6d704dbf9542b0a0830ec91a2db